# Grandfathered legacy files for scripts/forbid_stale_future_date_fixture.sh
#
# These test files carry absolute future-dated `DateTime.utc(...)` fixtures
# written BEFORE the stale-future-date gate existed. Most anchor logic that
# never reads `BookingDisplayX.isPast` (lane layout, slot repositories,
# mapper round-trips, timezone math) so they are not live time bombs today,
# but auditing and converting ~30 files in one pass was out of scope for the
# 2026-07-20 incident fix. They are frozen here so the gate is GREEN today
# while still blocking NEW absolute future literals in every other (and every
# freshly-authored) test file under the gate's scan roots. This is a
# RATCHET: when one of these files is next meaningfully edited, convert its
# `DateTime.utc(YYYY, ...)` literal(s) to `futureBookingStart()`
# (test/helpers/booking_fixture_dates.dart) — or annotate a genuinely
# deliberate fixed instant with `// future-date-ok: <reason>` — and DELETE
# its line here. The baseline only ever shrinks. One repo-relative path per
# line; paths from EITHER scan root (test/features/booking/,
# integration_test/) are valid entries.
#
# 2026-07-21: the scan was widened to `integration_test/`. NOTHING from that
# tree was added here — its five offending sites were each judged individually
# and resolved in place (two fixtures re-anchored to `fb.bookingStartsAt`,
# three genuinely date-pinned sites annotated `// future-date-ok:`). Widening
# a guard's reach and then allow-listing whatever it finds would reproduce
# exactly the blind spot the widening existed to close.
#
# Generated 2026-07-20 from the then-current corpus, immediately after fixing
# the four booking-detail specs whose expired anchor caused 16 real failures
# (booking_detail_screen_test.dart, booking_detail_interactions_test.dart,
# reschedule_in_flight_test.dart, booking_detail_provider_view_test.dart —
# NOT grandfathered; they're clean under the gate as of this commit).
